---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';

// About and Contact are one page, in that order. A one-person masthead and a
// way to reach that person are the same disclosure — splitting them across two
// routes made each half look thinner than it was.
//
// The old /contact channel block (editorial / tips / general, all pointing at
// the same mailbox) is gone: three buttons resolving to one address is
// theatre. One address, stated once.
const mailto = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`;
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Who's behind Vantage, what it stands for, and how to reach them."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <p class="text-[11.5px] font-semibold text-teal-light uppercase tracking-[0.09em] mb-3">About</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-display font-bold text-paper leading-tight mb-5">
      About Vantage
    </h1>

    <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper/70 text-justify hyphens-auto">
      <p>
        Vantage is a Philippine news and media company built on the idea contained in
        its name: what you understand depends on where you stand. We cover the issues
        the country is arguing about right now, and our work is to make those arguments
        legible: what is actually being proposed, who stands to gain or lose, and what
        has already been tried. We follow decisions from the offices where they are
        drafted to the communities where they land, in Metro Manila and well outside it.
        Being useful to our readers matters more to us than being first to publish.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are working toward a Philippines where public life is conducted in front of
        an informed audience, where the people affected by a decision understand it well
        enough to question it. That means building a newsroom Filipinos return to out of
        habit rather than accident, and producing journalism that still holds up a year
        after it runs. It also means treating our readers as participants rather than
        traffic: people with their own vantage points, whose questions shape what we
        pursue next.
      </p>
      <p>
        Accuracy is our first obligation, and we would rather be late than wrong. We
        report independently, without deference to advertisers, political patrons, or
        the pressure of a trending topic. We stay close to the ground, because distance
        is how stories get flattened into abstractions. We show our work: naming sources
        where we safely can, explaining how we know what we know, and correcting errors
        openly and quickly rather than quietly. And we write plainly, on the conviction
        that anything worth reporting can be explained clearly to anyone willing to read
        it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold text-paper mt-10 mb-4">Masthead</h2>
    <div class="bg-ink border border-paper/15 rounded-xl p-5 flex items-center gap-4">
      <img
        src="/masthead/jairus-macabuhay.jpg"
        alt="Sir Jairus Macabuhay"
        width="96"
        height="96"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-20 h-20 sm:w-24 sm:h-24 rounded-xl object-cover shrink-0 bg-ground"
      />
      <div>
        <p class="font-medium text-paper">Sir Jairus Macabuhay</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-paper/60 mt-0.5">Founder and Editor-in-Chief</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold text-paper mt-10 mb-4">Independence</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper/70 text-justify hyphens-auto">
      Vantage is self-funded. We receive no money from political parties, campaigns,
      government agencies, corporations, or advocacy groups, and no outside organization
      has any say in what we cover or how we cover it. If that ever changes, we will say
      so here, plainly and before you have to ask.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold text-paper mt-10 mb-4">Corrections</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper/70 text-justify hyphens-auto">
      When we get something wrong, we fix it and say what we fixed. Corrections are noted
      on the story itself, with the date and the nature of the error. Nothing gets quietly
      edited after publication.
    </p>

    <div class="border-t border-paper/10 mt-12 pt-10">
      <p class="text-[11.5px] font-semibold text-teal-light uppercase tracking-[0.09em] mb-3">Contact</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-display font-bold text-paper leading-tight mb-5">
        Get in touch
      </h2>

      {/* The one highlight moment on the page, and the only place the address */}
      {/* appears. Deliberately unlabelled by purpose: tips, questions and */}
      {/* corrections all land in the same inbox, so naming one of them would */}
      {/* imply the others belong somewhere else. */}
      <div class="bg-teal-light rounded-xl p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-teal-dark uppercase tracking-[0.08em] mb-2">Message us here</p>
        <a href={mailto} class="text-sm font-semibold text-teal-dark underline underline-offset-2">
          {CONTACT_EMAIL}
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
